  "worked_solution": "Notice that\n\n- $-{x}^{3}y$ is defined for all $x$ and $y,$ and\n\n- ${e}^{g(x,y)}$ is defined if $g(x,y)$ is defined.\n\nAs a result, ${e}^{-{x}^{3}y}$ is defined for all values of $x$ and $y.$ This means that the domain of $f$ is the entire $xy$-plane.",
